docs/specs/FAILURE-LEARNING-LOOP-SPEC.eli16.md:23:You shouldn't have to go digging, so there are three channels, deliberately ordered from quietest to most attention-grabbing:
docs/specs/FAILURE-LEARNING-LOOP-SPEC.eli16.md:26:2. **A quiet heads-up in your existing system topic** — when a real insight is discovered, I post *once*, into the channel you already have, the same calm way the watchdog alerts work — not a new buzzing topic (we learned that lesson the hard way), and never a ping per bug. Just "here's a pattern worth knowing, with the evidence," once, and it stays off by default until you switch it on. Using the topic you already have (rather than a brand-new one) is a deliberate decision, not something we're putting off — it's how we avoid re-introducing notification spam. This is the "tell me when you learn something" channel you asked for.
