docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:21:   The pinning test repeats the wrong table while claiming live-documentation verification ([telegram-send-funnel-invisible-payload.test.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/tests/unit/telegram-send-funnel-invisible-payload.test.ts:542)), disproving the spec’s assertion that this pin makes silent drift impossible ([spec](/Users/justin/window12-exam/docs/specs/telegram-egress-invisible-payload-guard.md:329)). This is an intersection of declared residuals, not a recount of either one alone.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:23:2. **DESIGN — the RichText walker is not the grammar; it traverses Telegram-ignored object members.**
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:25:   `structuredTextLeaves` loops through every property and recursively descends every object-valued property ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:432)). Telegram instead selects a `type` discriminator and extracts only that variant’s defined fields before returning; for example, URL consumes `text` and `url`, while reference consumes `text` and `name` ([official parser](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api/blob/master/telegram-bot-api/Client.cpp#L11326-L11443)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:27:   Concrete failure path: a valid wrapper has an invisible real label and an extra, server-ignored nested member containing a visible-looking `text` leaf. The door counts the ignored leaf and allows; Telegram discards it and renders only the invisible label.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:31:3. **DESIGN — mathematical expressions are checked as source code, not rendered content.**
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:35:   The walker classifies `expression` as an ordinary unformatted string ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:432)), then accepts it whenever source characters satisfy the Unicode predicate ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:464)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:37:   Concrete failure path: a valid layout/spacing-only LaTeX expression contains letters or punctuation in its source but paints no visible glyph. The source passes while the rendered message is empty. This extends CMT-1260 beyond its stated HTML/Markdown scope.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:51:   The comment’s concrete failure path does not exist: a visible reference label is already walked through `text`. Applying the suggested discriminator repair to count `name` would instead count a non-rendered identifier and could introduce an under-refusal.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:63:- **Redirect crossing:** Still open exactly as described. Classification occurs once from the initial URL ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:36)); final `fetch` retains default redirect following.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:65:- **Encoding inferred from wrapper rather than `Content-Type`:** Still open. `collectParams` branches only on body value/type ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:215)) and never reads headers.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:67:- **Irrelevant duplicated JSON keys:** Still open as an over-refusal. Any top-level duplicate makes the whole body unreadable before relevance is considered ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:217)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:69:- **`answerCallbackQuery`:** Still a stated product judgment rather than a mechanical no-content fact; it remains bodyless ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:176)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:71:- **`editForumTopic`:** Still guarded unconditionally through `name`; empty-name/preserve-current semantics remain unmodeled ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:140)).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:73:- **Local Bot API Server:** Still outside runtime and lint recognition because both hard-code `api.telegram.org` ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:60), [lint](/Users/justin/window12-exam/scripts/lint-telegram-egress-boundary.mjs:48)). Telegram supports replacing the cloud endpoint with a [local server](https://github.com/tdlib/telegram-bot-api#moving-a-bot-to-a-local-server).
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:77:- **Single-read claim:** Still false. `{ ...init }` invokes an enumerable `body` getter again ([telegram-egress.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/telegram-egress.ts:427)). The test checks only the final outgoing body, not the getter count ([telegram-egress-boundary.test.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/tests/unit/telegram-egress-boundary.test.ts:275)). The captured value overwrites the second result, so this is now a claim/side-effect defect rather than the old direct body swap.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:81:- **Structured content only in JSON bodies:** Still open. Query/form/multipart collection leaves `rich_message` as a JSON-serialized string, after which JSON punctuation satisfies the scalar predicate.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:87:- **No-leaf structures:** Still open and unsafe. All no-leaf objects are allowed ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:464)), but the union contains both visible media/dividers and non-rendered anchors. Telegram expressly permits an empty named anchor.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:95:- **Rendering shortcut / CMT-1260:** Still open. HTML/Markdown are locally approximated ([invisible-payload.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:298)); the stated malformed-tag over-refusal and encoded/delimiter under-refusals remain. Its description is incomplete because LaTeX adds Finding 3.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:99:- **Runtime Unicode table / CMT-1261:** Still open. The predicate uses runtime property escapes and records the engine/version but does not pin or vendor the table.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:103:- **Blinded door and aliased fetch:** Still open. The lint explicitly does not validate method-recovery behavior or follow a fetch reference stored under another name. Its categorical clean output therefore remains broader than its analysis.
docs/specs/reports/window10-external-passes/pass47-verdict.md:105:- **Deliberately red family audit:** The assertion still expects `current` while comments identify Building and The Substrate as stale ([standards-coverage-ratchet.test.ts](/Users/justin/window12-exam/tests/unit/standards-coverage-ratchet.test.ts:906)). Runtime confirmation was unavailable because this copy lacks `js-yaml` and `typescript`; consequently, the standards script, boundary lint, and test suite could not execute. Static inspection confirms the red expectation remains.
docs/specs/emergency-stop-forward-path-wiring.eli16.md:5:If you type "stop everything" to me right now, nothing actually stops me. The message just gets handed to me like any other note. There's a real kill-switch built into instar — a detector that spots "stop"/"cancel"/"halt" and immediately kills the running session — but it's wired into the wrong door.
docs/specs/emergency-stop-forward-path-wiring.eli16.md:20:1. **Fail-open.** If the detector ever hiccups or errors, the message just gets delivered normally — the safety check can *never* block your messages from reaching me. The worst a bug in this code can do is "behave like today."
docs/specs/emergency-stop-forward-path-wiring.eli16.md:29:A small, localized change to one server route, fail-open by design, that makes "stop everything" actually stop me regardless of which door my messages come through — plus the test that keeps it that way. I'll prove it with a real before/after: confirm "stop everything" is ignored today, apply the fix, then confirm it terminates a live session.
