docs/specs/gemini-stuck-input-prompt-detection.eli16.md:1:# ELI16 — recognize Gemini's input box so stuck messages get auto-recovered
docs/specs/gemini-stuck-input-prompt-detection.eli16.md:5:That function looked for the cursor by checking the line for a prompt character: `❯` (Claude Code) or `›` (codex). **Gemini CLI uses neither.** Gemini draws its input inside a rounded border, and the active input line looks like `│ * <your text>` (a box pipe plus a bullet). Because `isMarkerStuckAtPrompt` didn't recognize that shape, it always concluded a Gemini message was *not* stuck — so the Enter-recovery never fired for Gemini, and forwarded prompts stalled in the box until something else nudged them. This is the recurring "Gemini auto-submit" friction the mentee layer kept hitting (rc=2 in the framework-issue ledger); it bit the loop live this session — a message to Codey sat unsubmitted until I manually sent Enter.
