docs/specs/wall-is-a-hypothesis-standard.eli16.md:27:While building this, I checked whether the constitution's claim that "a new rule starts being enforced the moment it's written" was actually true in the code. It isn't yet — the automatic enforcers it describes are still future plans. So instead of pretending, I wired the rule into the two places that are real today: the message checker above, and the one document my spec-review process actually reads. That way the rule has teeth now, and I'm not making a claim I haven't verified — which is the whole point of the rule.
