docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:2:title: "Feature Maturation D7 — recurring measurable evaluation on the shared metrics substrate"
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:11:rollout-criteria: "seven-day development-agent soak; every eligible rollout evaluated when due under its declared cadence; zero missed-due rows; no authority or blocker-state mutation"
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:22:contested-then-cleared: 0
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:96:| Evaluation eligibility | `dark|dry-run|live` | Non-terminal stages re-scored; `default-on` retains history only. |
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:97:| D7's own rollout flag | `monitoring.blockerLifecycleLedger` | Whether this measurement substrate runs on the current agent; unrelated to a measured feature's stage. |
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:157:The feature list is stable-sorted and capped at 512. `missedDue` counts eligible features with no durable evaluation in their current cadence slot. A failed write therefore remains visibly missed; it is never inferred as healthy.
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:171:### Alternatives considered
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:181:No credentials, hardware identities, or user-visible URLs are introduced.
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:187:- Per-metric pass — `invariant`: fixed direction/threshold/sample/freshness comparison declared by the feature.
docs/specs/feature-maturation-recurring-evaluation.md:229:14. Query-plan tests assert all newest-observation, current-slot, and trend reads use the declared indexes and preserve the 512 × 16 bound.
