docs/specs/auto-updater-lifeline-coordination.eli16.md:3:> **One-line shape:** when the server auto-updates across a breaking version boundary, the lifeline gets restarted at the same time. The fact that we shipped four of five fixes two days ago and deferred this one is exactly the pattern that bit us again today — so this PR also adds a structural check that blocks future deferrals.
docs/specs/auto-updater-lifeline-coordination.eli16.md:23:**Layer 5 — the meta-fix: structural no-deferrals enforcement.** The instar-dev pre-commit gate now scans the spec for "deferred / out of scope today / follow-up / preemptive fix" patterns. If a deferral isn't linked to a tracked commitment ID, the commit is blocked. This is the structural answer to today's feedback ("we need to change how we develop"). It moves the "no deferrals" rule from my head into the hook system where it can't be forgotten.
docs/specs/auto-updater-lifeline-coordination.eli16.md:27:Two days ago we shipped four fixes and deferred one. That deferral produced today's regression. The lesson is structural, not motivational: deferrals breed incompleteness. So:
