docs/specs/self-heal-gate.eli16.md:9:The first real use fixes a current warning-only gap. A development checkout can discover that its generated feedback-factory defaults are missing or stale. Today it logs that automatic repair is deferred. After this change, the local canonical owner can repair that specific file through SelfHealGate using the already-existing defaults writer, hardened against unsafe paths and partial writes. Missing or stale data is recoverable. Malformed, unreadable, symlinked, or otherwise uncertain data is not overwritten; it immediately creates an operator notice.
docs/specs/self-heal-gate.eli16.md:13:This first consumer is local by design because the file configures one physical source checkout. The local episode store does not claim to become shared merely because the governor knows about multiple machines. A future pool-wide repair must use a truly shared episode store or route every attempt through one fenced owner, and the declaration rejects a local store for a pool-shared controller.
