docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:5:1. The Body and the Mind — a consequential decision can escape the mind by escaping the declaration population — a new tier/owner/safety classifier that is never declared is invisible to the proposed guard over “each declared decision point,” so structure can make the same context-poor judgment as the tier classifier in the earned incident.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:6:2. Structure Decides Alone Only on an Exact Match — a genuine halt outside the enumerated wording is lost when the model is unavailable — “halt all work now” misses the exact list, the unavailable model cannot add the inferred stop, and execution continues; the article explicitly accepts that degraded coverage rather than providing a safe emergency path.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:14:10. Quantitative Claims Must Bind a Subject — subject confusion is covered only for the first time verifier — a coverage percentage for a test corpus is treated as fleet coverage by another quantitative verifier; the paired decision table in `time-claim.ts` never runs, and no family-wide subject-binding guard is named.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:15:11. The Agent Is Always Reachable — the guaranteed floor does not cover the path that carries messages to the live session — the ingress long-poller can die while the lifeline remains live, satisfying the session/resource predicate while the operator still cannot reach it; the article explicitly excludes this layer and cites only a separate, unbound guarantee.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:18:14. The Right to Stand Ground — the trained capitulation path is wholly open — an unsupported reviewer objection arrives, no reversal/evidence record is required, and the agent agrees reflexively; the article admits no structural surface, so reviewer unavailability or gate absence changes nothing because there is no machinery to fail safe.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:19:15. A Wall Is a Hypothesis — a false wall can be enacted without ever being declared — a design silently omits `/goal` delegation and chooses a manual alternative without emitting “no API” or another defeat phrase; B16 and the spec reviewer see no feasibility claim, so the earned recommendation ships again through omission.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:20:16. Never a False Blocker — a false human dependency can be stored internally without crossing the outbound gate — a work item is marked `blocked-on-user` and idles without sending a blocker-flavoured message; B17 and its pre-tool signal never evaluate the state, leaving the button-the-agent-could-click failure reachable.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:24:20. Remove What Demands Attention. Do Not Supply More Attention. — the crystallizing duplicate-prose failure remains outside the guard — the same count is copied into two paragraphs or two plan files, one copy is updated, and `lint-no-duplicate-definitions` stays green because it checks structured registry definitions, not duplicated facts.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r5.out:26:22. A Dispatch Supplies the Question and Withholds the Answer — the exact earned path bypasses the enforcement chokepoint — an ad-hoc shell/heredoc dispatch includes “expected: empty,” anchors the checker, and never touches the template lint; the article explicitly says this is how the crystallizing failure happened.
