docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass39.out:37:   `answerCallbackQuery` is classified as bodyless at `src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:164-174` because omitted or empty text may dismiss the spinner, although `:117-123` admits it has reader-visible text. Telegram documents `text` as its notification body and `show_alert` as selecting an alert ([Bot API](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#answercallbackquery)). A dynamic handler result reaches this method at `src/messaging/TelegramAdapter.ts:5461-5472`.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass39.out:41:   The inverse defect exists for `editForumTopic`, mapped unconditionally to `name` at `src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:125-139`. Telegram documents an empty name as preserving the current name ([Bot API](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#editforumtopic)). An icon-only edit carrying an empty name is therefore wrongly refused.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass39.out:57:   Concrete failure path: a visible query value accompanied by an ignored byte-oriented body is decidable and deliverable, yet rejected. Valid JSON bytes carried by a Blob or fresh Request are likewise destroyed.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass39.out:59:7. **DESIGN — the new Request refusal is absent from the structured decision stream.**
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass39.out:83:   Concrete failure path: a maintainer following the governing acceptance or rollback sections searches for nonexistent guard calls and ratchets, or attributes predecessor properties to the current boundary. The summary’s broad warning at `:50-57` does not make these unlabelled governing sections true or safely historical.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/pass39.out:91:3. **Still open as described.** Runtime property escapes remain at `src/messaging/invisible-payload.ts:64` and `:77`; the vendored table remains assigned to CMT-1261 at `:83-89`.
