docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r2.out:6:2. Deferral = Deletion — “Anything worth keeping” must be captured now, but whether evidence is worth keeping can become knowable only afterward — “an anomalous log line looks harmless during a healthy run and becomes the sole clue after tomorrow’s outage.”
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r2.out:10:6. Name the Gravity Wells — “Enumerate the predictable self-deceptions” names no responsible enumerator and supplies no point at which a trap becomes predictably enumerable — “a routine model upgrade introduces a new helpfulness bias that cannot be named until instances have already exhibited it.”
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r2.out:13:9. The Operator Channel Is Sacred — The claim that a missed inbound “pause” is benign makes its delivery-first rule unsafe when applied literally — “pause before sending the remaining 500 emails” is phrased outside the exact-match set, reaches a busy agent instead of stopping the sender, and more irreversible messages leave before the agent handles it.
docs/specs/reports/window12-laptop/substrate-r2.out:14:10. Session Input Is a Principal — At the moment untagged input arrives, the session lacks the very provenance required to decide whether it is a genuine driver instruction or impersonation — “the real driver sends an urgent untagged correction”; accepting it violates principal verification, while refusing it discards legitimate operator control.
